# Installed by pass's top-level install.sh at /etc/pam.d/pass-howdy.
#
# An isolated PAM service used only by pass-howdy (see
# pass-howdy/src/lib.rs) to gate "unlock with your face" — it is never
# referenced by sudo, login, or any other system authentication path, and
# nothing else on this system should be pointed at it.
#
# `sufficient`: a successful face match (via howdy) immediately succeeds
# the whole stack, no further modules consulted. `required pam_deny.so`:
# anything else (no face match, no camera, howdy misconfigured) always
# denies — deliberately no fallback to a system password prompt here;
# pass's own master-password prompt is the fallback, one layer up.
auth sufficient __PAM_HOWDY_MODULE_PATH__
auth required pam_deny.so

# No actual account/session state to manage for this service, but PAM
# requires every applicable module type to resolve to something.
account required pam_permit.so
